# Dapta Project Context

Before planning, implementing, evaluating, or pitching this project, read
`docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`. Treat it as the durable source of project intent and
update it when the team makes a consequential decision or produces new verified
evidence.

Core guardrails:

- Dapta compiles stable, repetitive, evaluable AI workflows into verified,
  hot-swappable LoRA specialists on a shared open-weight base model.
- Keep measured facts, proposed architecture, illustrative economics, and future
  vision explicitly separated.
- Do not claim that LoRA removes inference, tools, reasoning, or all runtime cost.
- Do not claim latency or dollar-cost wins until they are measured defensibly.
- Preserve frozen held-out tests and prefer deterministic ground truth wherever
  the workflow permits it.
- Route uncertain, unfamiliar, dynamic, or tool-dependent work to the general
  path or human review rather than forcing a specialist.
- The old `skill2lora` repository is source material and a proven POC; migration
  into this repository must be planned before files are copied or rewritten.
